\begingroup
\newminted[MDCode]{d}{}
\begin{MDCode}
auto pair = ch('a') & ch('b');
auto alternate = try_parse(pair) | (ch('a') & ch('c'));
assert(!run_parser(alternate, "ac").value.isNull);
auto digits = satisfy((char c) => c >= '0' && c <= '9', "digit").many();
assert(run_parser(digits, "123").value.get == ['1', '2', '3']);
\end{MDCode}
\endgroup

Inspect \texttt{v\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}N\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}l} and \texttt{e\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}r} on a \texttt{P\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}O\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}e}. Failures distinguish \texttt{S\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}t} and \texttt{C\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}d}; \texttt{t\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}y\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e} restores the cursor and softens a failure. Repetition rejects successful parsers that consume no input. \texttt{p\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}w\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}h\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n} passes a \texttt{P\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}S\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}e} span to a user callback; \texttt{p\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}d\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}!\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}d\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{})} stores a compile-time production identifier with its handler.

PEG combinators are \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}q}, \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}h\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}e}, \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}t}, \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}y}, \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}y\allowbreak{}1}, \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}d}, \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}t}, \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}e}, and \texttt{p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}h\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}l}. \texttt{c\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}d\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{})} and \texttt{d\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}v\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}d\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{})} return reference-type definitions. \texttt{a\allow