\section{Tasks and shared state}

\texttt{T\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}k\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{},\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}b\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}k\allowbreak{})} takes a \texttt{r\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}T\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}k\allowbreak{}S\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e} callback returning \texttt{R\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}!\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{},\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{})}. \texttt{t\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}k\allowbreak{}1\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}|\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}k\allowbreak{}2} creates a \texttt{T\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}k\allowbreak{}C\allowbreak{}h\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n}; \texttt{r\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}n} records each result by task name. Policies are \texttt{S\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}O\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}E\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}r} and \texttt{C\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}O\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}E\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}r}. \texttt{s\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}d\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{})} stops subsequent work; \texttt{u\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n} runs a task when a supplied event callable returns true. Stateful caches, lazy values and PEG objects do not provide synchronization.

\section{Native enum reflection}

\begingroup
\newminted[MDCode]{d}{}
\begin{MDCode}
enum Color { Red = -1000, Green = 0, AliasGreen = 0, Blue = 1000 }
static assert(enum_count!Color() == 3);
static assert(enum_name!(Color.Red)() == "Red");
static assert(enum_values!Color() == [Color.Red, Color.Green, Color.Blue]);
auto blue = enum_cast!Color("blue", case_insensitive);
assert(blue.get == Color.Blue);
auto name = enum_switch!((c) => enum_name!(typeof(c).value)())(Color.Blue);
assert(name == "Blue");
\end{MDCode}
\endgroup

Declared members are reflected without numeric search-range limits. Values are sorted numerically and duplicate values use the first declared name. Checked casts/\allowbreak{}indexing and adjacency return \texttt{N\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}b\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}e}; arrays of values, names and entries are returned as fixed-size values. \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}d\allowbreak{}!\allowbreak{}E\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{})} checks reflected membership in D. \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}w\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}h} has an optional fallback; its no-fallback form raises an exception for an unknown value.

\begingroup
\newminted[MDCode]{d}{}
\begin{MDCode}
@(EnumOptions(true)) enum Access { Read = 1, Write = 2, Execute = 4, All = 7 }
assert(enum_flags_name(Access.Read | Access.Write) == "Read|Write");
@(EnumOptions(false, 2)) @(EnumNames(["c_Red": "rouge"]))
enum Named { c_Red, c_Blue }
static assert(enum_name(Named.c_Red) == "rouge");
static assert(enum_name(Named.c_Blue) == "Blue");
\end{MDCode}
\endgroup

\texttt{E\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}O\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}s} sets flags mode and prefix trimming; \texttt{E\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}N\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}s} maps declaration names to display names. Flags reflection selects single-bit members. Helpers include \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}t}, \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}s}, \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}t}, and \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}g\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}y}. \texttt{E\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}A\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}y\allowbreak{}!\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}E\allowbreak{},\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}V\allowbreak{})}, \texttt{E\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}B\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}!\allowbreak{}E}, and \texttt{E\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}S\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}!\allowbreak{}E} supply enum-indexed containers. D's native enum formatting/\allowbreak{}bitwise operators supply the host-language integrations. Chapter 29 documents C++'s upstream-specific configuration, namespace aliases and stream/\allowbreak{}formatter APIs.

